+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Asks for the connection's authenticated user's own conversations (re-cinq/HALEngine#144). The frame has no user id field: the list is always the connection's user's.
+
+- `limit`, when present, is an integer 1-200 and `before`, when present, a string `Date.parse` accepts; anything else is `INVALID_MESSAGE` naming the field ([validated by: accepts a bare list_conversations and names the field of any bad limit or before](../../src/transport/conversationListFrame.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- It is answered with one `conversation_list` frame of the connecting user's summaries, newest first, with ISO-string times, taken from `ws.userId` and never from the frame ([validated by: answers the connecting user their own conversations, newest first, whatever userId the frame carries](../../src/transport/conversationListFrame.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
+- With `transport.history` off, or a store that cannot list, it is answered with one `error` frame coded `UNSUPPORTED` and never an empty list ([validated by: answers one UNSUPPORTED error, never a list, when history is off or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/conversationListFrame.acceptance.test.ts#L121)).
+- It is answered off the per-session lock, so it does not wait for a streaming turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a list request while a user_message is still streaming, before its stream_end](../../src/transport/conversationListFrame.acceptance.test.ts#L137)).
+
